{{also|schiefer}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schiver}}, from {{inh|de|goh|skivaro}}. Related with {{m|de|Scheibe}} and {{m|de|scheiden}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃiːfɐ/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schiefer.ogg}}
* {{homophone|de|schiefer}}
* Some western German speakers distinguish {{m|de||schiefer}} with {{IPAchar|/v/}} from {{m|de||Schiefer}} with {{IPAchar|/f/}}. However, very conservative speakers may have {{IPAchar|/v/}} in both.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m}}

# [[shale]], [[slate]]
#: {{syn|de|Lei|q=obsolete}}
# {{lb|de|Austria|Bavaria}} small [[splinter]] {{gloss|sharp piece of wood, etc.}}
#: {{syn|de|Splitter}}
#: {{ux|de|sich einen '''Schiefer''' einziehen|to get a '''splinter''' into one's finger by accident}}

